<h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">Consulting</h1>

<div class="space-y-8">
  <p class="text-lg">
    I occasionally take on short, focused engagements outside my day job. The work is limited in scope
    and time so it stays secondary to both employment and the open-source / writing side of things.
  </p>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">What I can help with</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3">
      <li>
        Making HTTP clients and network-facing code more reliable in production: timeouts, retries,
        circuit breaking, bulkheads, and observable failure modes.
      </li>
      <li>
        Designing and reviewing chaos / fault-injection approaches for services and tests.
      </li>
      <li>
        Backend and distributed-systems questions around failure handling, consistency edges, and
        operational reality.
      </li>
      <li>
        Turning fuzzy reliability requirements into concrete design and implementation choices.
      </li>
      <li>
        Building and reviewing RAG pipelines - ingestion and chunking, embeddings, vector and hybrid
        search, ranking, and keeping an index fresh, fast, and useful once it is in production.
      </li>
      <li>
        Choosing the right database for a workload: knowing when a general-purpose engine is enough and
        when a specialist (vector, time-series, graph, columnar/OLAP, geospatial) has truly earned its
        place, and how to combine them into a hybrid architecture that stays operationally sane. This is
        the subject of my forthcoming book,
        <a href="/publications/database-safari/">The Database Safari</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p class="text-lg">
    Basically the same territory as my <a href="https://gaborkoos.com">portfolio</a>, the <a href="/">writing</a>, and the
    <a href="/code">libraries</a>: reliability under real conditions, especially around networking and
    asynchronous work.
  </p>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">How it usually works</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3">
      <li>
        Short advisory calls or reviews (design, code, test strategy).
      </li>
      <li>
        Small implementation or pairing blocks when that is the fastest way to unblock something.
      </li>
      <li>
        Fixed scope preferred over open-ended obligations.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Availability</h2>
    <p>
      Limited. I only take work that fits cleanly around existing commitments so I can actually deliver.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    If you have a concrete problem in the areas above, email me at 
    <a href="mailto:gabor@gaborkoos.com">gabor@gaborkoos.com</a> with a short description of the
    situation and what you want out of the engagement. I will reply if it looks like a fit.
  </p>
</div>
